WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.800
Next, we are going to talk about infant CPR,

00:00:02.800 --> 00:00:05.640
which applies to any baby up to one year old.

00:00:05.640 --> 00:00:08.740
Much like with older children, cardiac arrest in infants

00:00:08.740 --> 00:00:11.260
usually starts as a respiratory issue

00:00:11.260 --> 00:00:13.080
rather than a heart problem.

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:14.780
While the situation is different,

00:00:14.780 --> 00:00:17.200
you will find that the core steps of the rescue

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:20.219
remain the same ones you have already learned.

00:00:20.219 --> 00:00:24.040
One, ensure the scene is safe before you approach.

00:00:24.040 --> 00:00:27.480
Two, assess the infant for responsiveness.

00:00:27.480 --> 00:00:30.240
Because a baby can't tell you if they are okay,

00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:31.719
you will check for a reaction

00:00:31.719 --> 00:00:35.080
by tickling the infant's foot or pinching their toe.

00:00:35.080 --> 00:00:37.639
While you do this, check for breathing.

00:00:37.639 --> 00:00:40.779
Is their chest rising and falling?

00:00:40.779 --> 00:00:43.919
Look for those severe signs we discussed earlier,

00:00:43.919 --> 00:00:47.820
a lack of consciousness or blue lips and extremities.

00:00:47.820 --> 00:00:50.040
If the baby moves when you tickle their foot,

00:00:50.040 --> 00:00:51.560
that is a great sign,

00:00:51.560 --> 00:00:53.720
but you should still call 911

00:00:53.720 --> 00:00:56.040
if you feel something is wrong.

00:00:56.080 --> 00:00:59.759
Three, call for help and activate 911.

00:00:59.759 --> 00:01:03.040
If the infant is unresponsive and not breathing,

00:01:03.040 --> 00:01:06.800
call 911 immediately and place them on speakerphone

00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:10.559
so you can begin CPR while talking to the dispatcher.

00:01:10.559 --> 00:01:12.559
There is one major difference for infants

00:01:12.559 --> 00:01:14.959
if you are alone and do not have a phone.

00:01:14.959 --> 00:01:18.120
You should perform five rounds of CPR first.

00:01:18.120 --> 00:01:21.339
If the baby is still unresponsive after those rounds,

00:01:21.339 --> 00:01:23.279
pick the baby up and take them with you

00:01:23.279 --> 00:01:25.040
to find a phone or help.

00:01:25.040 --> 00:01:27.120
You never want to leave an infant alone

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:28.720
while you go to get assistance.

